Package: z3r
Title: Native R Interface to the Z3 Theorem Prover
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: An interface to the 'Z3' satisfiability modulo theories (SMT)
    solver <https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3> built directly on its native C
    API. Provides typed symbolic expressions over integers, exact rationals,
    Booleans, bit-vectors, IEEE floating point, arrays, sets, strings,
    sequences, regular expressions, algebraic datatypes and uninterpreted
    functions, with natural R operator syntax; solvers with incremental
    solving, assumptions, unsatisfiable cores and proofs; optimization with
    objectives and weighted soft constraints; quantifiers, recursive
    functions, tactics, probes and simplifiers; constrained Horn clauses;
    real closed fields and algebraic numbers; user propagators; and
    'SMT-LIB2' import and export. Exact values are never silently rounded to
    double precision. This is an independent third-party package; it is not
    an official 'Z3' or Microsoft product.
License: GPL-3
